Container definitions read by `/usr/bin/podman-stack update`.

One .conf file per container, in sh assignment form:

    NAME=SmartDNS
    IMAGE=docker.io/pymumu/smartdns:latest
    create() {
        podman create --name "$NAME" \
            --network=host --restart=always --cap-add=NET_RAW \
            --volume smartdns-conf:/etc/smartdns \
            "$IMAGE"
    }

create() has to be written out by hand because podman offers no primitive
that rebuilds a container in place on a new image. `podman auto-update` only
recognises the PODMAN_SYSTEMD_UNIT label a quadlet writes, and
`podman container clone` silently drops --network=host (the clone comes back
on bridge) and every --cap-add, leaving a container that cannot start here.
So update can only re-create from the original arguments given here.

This directory ships empty, so update does nothing by default. watchdog needs
no definitions and works on any running container that has a health probe.
